🔥 Playwright Test Framework – Strong Advantages over Selenium + TestNG

1️⃣ Faster and More Reliable Execution

Playwright communicates directly with browsers without the WebDriver layer and includes built-in auto waits for elements, network calls, and page states. This reduces latency, eliminates flaky tests, and delivers significantly faster execution compared to Selenium.

⸻

2️⃣ Native Parallel Execution at Scale

Playwright supports built-in parallel test execution without Selenium Grid or complex setup, enabling large test suites to finish much faster.

⸻

3️⃣ Lower Maintenance with Smart Locators

Playwright’s role-based and text-based locators are resilient to UI changes, reducing frequent script breakages caused by XPath-heavy Selenium tests.

⸻

4️⃣ Rapid Test Creation using CodeGen + GitHub Copilot

Playwright CodeGen records real user actions and generates working test scripts instantly, while GitHub Copilot helps refactor this code into clean, reusable methods and page objects, accelerating scalable automation.

⸻

5️⃣ Faster Debugging with Inspector, Debugger & Trace Viewer

Playwright provides Inspector, step-through debugging, and Trace Viewer with screenshots, DOM snapshots, network logs, and video—making root-cause analysis far faster than Selenium logs.

⸻

6️⃣ AI-Assisted Fixes & Continuous Improvements with GitHub Copilot

GitHub Copilot automatically suggests fixes, refactors, and required code changes when tests fail or application behavior changes, significantly reducing manual maintenance effort.

⸻

7️⃣ AI-Accelerated Migration with Playwright APIs + Copilot

Playwright’s modern APIs make scripts clear and maintainable, and GitHub Copilot can analyze existing Selenium TestNG tests and convert them into optimized Playwright code, reducing manual effort, shortening migration timelines, and modernizing legacy tests.

⸻

8️⃣ Built-In Reporting for Leadership Visibility

Playwright offers rich HTML reports with retries, screenshots, videos, and execution history out of the box, eliminating the need for additional reporting tools.

⸻

9️⃣ Lower Total Cost of Ownership (TCO)

Faster execution, reduced flakiness, minimal setup, built-in tooling, and AI-assisted maintenance make Playwright more cost-effective for long-term enterprise automation.
